  "output": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Three open decisions — positions from Priya and Sam</title>\n<style>\n  :root {\n    --ink: #1a1a1a;\n    --mute: #5c5c5c;\n    --rule: #d8d4cc;\n    --paper: #fbfaf7;\n    --accent: #7a3b2e;\n    --box: #fff;\n    --open: #8a5a00;\n  }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    background: var(--paper);\n    color: var(--ink);\n    font: 16px/1.6 Georgia, \"Iowan Old Style\", \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n  }\n  .wrap { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 24px 96px; }\n  header { border-bottom: 3px double var(--rule); padding-bottom: 24px; margin-bottom: 36px; }\n  h1 { font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 10px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }\n  .sub { color: var(--mute); font-size: 15px; margin: 0; }\n  h2 {\n    font-size: 21px; margin: 0 0 4px; letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  }\n  h3 { font-size: 15px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--mute); margin: 28px 0 10px; font-weight: 600; }\n  section.item { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 30px; margin-top: 40px; }\n  .tag {\n    display: inline-block; font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--open);\n    border: 1px solid var(--open); border-radius: 2px; padding: 1px 6px;\n    vertical-align: 3px; margin-right: 8px;\n  }\n  p { margin: 0 0 14px; }\n  .settled, .contested { padding-left: 16px; border-left: 3px solid var(--rule); }\n  .contested { border-left-color: var(--accent); }\n  blockquote {\n    margin: 16px 0; padding: 12px 18px; background: #f3f0e9;\n    border-left: 3px solid var(--rule); font-size: 15px; color: #3a3a3a;\n  }\n  pre {\n    background: #f1eee7; border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 12px 14px;\n    overflow-x: auto; font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n    margin: 0 0 14px;\n  }\n  code { font: 13px ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; background: #f1eee7; padding: 1px 4px; }\n  ul { margin: 0 0 14px; padding-left: 22px; }\n  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }\n  form { font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; }\n  fieldset {\n    border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--box);\n    padding: 16px 18px; margin: 18px 0 0; border-radius: 3px;\n  }\n  legend { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; padding: 0 8px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }\n  .who { display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; font-size: 15px; }\n  label.opt {\n    display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start;\n    font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; padding: 7px 0; cursor: pointer;\n  }\n  label.opt input { margin-top: 4px; flex: none; }\n  label.opt span b { font-weight: 600; }\n  textarea {\n    width: 100%; min-height: 84px; margin-top: 8px; padding: 9px 10px;\n    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px; background: #fff;\n    font: 14px/1.55 system-ui, sans-serif; resize: vertical;\n  }\n  input[type=text] {\n    padding: 7px 9px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 3px;\n    font: 14px system-ui, sans-serif; width: 100%; max-width: 340px;\n  }\n  .hint { font-size: 13px; color: var(--mute); font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 4px 0 0; }\n  .row { display: flex; gap: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n  .row > div { flex: 1 1 240px; }\n  .actions { margin-top: 34px; display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }\n  button {\n    font: 15px system-ui, sans-serif; padding: 10px 18px; border-radius: 3px;\n    border: 1px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent); color: #fff; cursor: pointer;\n  }\n  button.ghost { background: transparent; color: var(--accent); }\n  button:hover { opacity: 0.88; }\n  #out { display: none; margin-top: 26px; }\n  #out textarea { min-height: 300px; font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; }\n  footer { margin-top: 60px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 16px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--mute); font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  @media print { button, .actions, #out { display: none !important; } body { background: #fff; } }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n\n<header>\n  <h1>Three open decisions in <code>docs/DESIGN.md</code></h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">The argument as it stands, plus a position required from Priya and Sam on each item. Nothing below is settled by writing it down — the <span class=\"tag\">OPEN</span> markers are the author's, and each one is a live question.</p>\n</header>\n\n<p>Three things are marked open in the design doc. They are not independent: item&nbsp;1 decides whether the service should exist in its current shape, item&nbsp;2 decides whether it can be pointed at anyone outside the team, and item&nbsp;3 decides how agents reach it. A \"no\" on item&nbsp;1 makes the other two moot, so answer it first even if you feel weakest on it.</p>\n\n<!-- ITEM 1 -->\n<section class=\"item\">\n  <h2><span class=\"tag\">OPEN&nbsp;1</span>The core bet: a schema, not a framework</h2>\n\n  <h3>What the doc asserts</h3>\n  <div class=\"settled\">\n    <p>Generating bespoke HTML costs thousands of output tokens every time, and that generation — not context loading, not deploy latency — is where the current approach is slow and expensive. So the agent-facing surface is a <b>schema the agent emits against</b>, not a framework it programs against:</p>\n    <pre>{\"type\": \"decision-matrix\", \"options\": [...], \"criteria\": [...]}</pre>\n    <p>The claim is a 20–50× token reduction over an authored page, and that reduction is stated as \"the entire reason this service exists.\" The corollary: any design decision that pushes agents back toward writing markup has broken the bet.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h3>What is contested</h3>\n  <div class=\"contested\">\n    <blockquote>Worth confirming against two or three real past generations before committing. If the dominant cost turns out to be context loading rather than generation, the answer is a cached design doc, not this service.</blockquote>\n    <p>So the 20–50× figure is currently an estimate carrying the whole architecture. The doc names its own falsifier — a measurement that shows context loading dominates — and names the alternative that would win instead. The open question is whether to spend the measurement before building further, and who does it.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <legend>Item 1 — your position</legend>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"Confirm as stated — build on the bet now\"><span><b>Confirm as stated.</b> The reasoning is sound enough; build on the schema bet without a measurement gate.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"Measure first — 2-3 past generations before further commitment\"><span><b>Measure first.</b> Pull two or three real past generations and check generation cost against context cost before committing further work.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"Measure, but in parallel — do not block build\"><span><b>Measure in parallel.</b> Do the check, but don't hold the build behind it.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"Context loading dominates — cached design doc, not this service\"><span><b>The bet is wrong.</b> I already believe context loading dominates; the answer is a cached design doc, not this service.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q1\" value=\"Other (see reasoning)\"><span><b>Other</b> — see my reasoning.</span></label>\n    <textarea name=\"q1why\" placeholder=\"Why. If you want the measurement, say what number would change your mind and who runs it.\"></textarea>\n  </fieldset>\n</section>\n\n<!-- ITEM 2 -->\n<section class=\"item\">\n  <h2><span class=\"tag\">OPEN&nbsp;2</span>The per-dev cluster problem</h2>\n\n  <h3>The situation</h3>\n  <div class=\"settled\">\n    <p>Every dev runs an independent single-node k3s cluster behind their own tunnel. A participant link therefore points at <i>that dev's box</i>. A stakeholder who clicks it six hours later gets an answer only if the box is still up — and the box is also a NixOS host that gets rebuilt.</p>\n    <p>The doc's own read: for a dev-phase tool this is <i>probably</i> tolerable — the boxes are always-on and the blast radius is one dev's briefs. It is explicitly <b>not</b> tolerable if links go to people outside the team, \"because a dead link to an external stakeholder is worse than never having sent one.\"</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h3>Insurance already taken</h3>\n  <div class=\"settled\">\n    <p><b>Never bake the host into a brief's identity.</b> A handle plus a participant token identify a brief; the hostname serving it is deployment configuration. Costs nothing today, and keeps \"move to one shared deployment\" a config change rather than a migration.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h3>What is contested</h3>\n  <div class=\"contested\">\n    <p>Whether \"internal links only\" is a rule anyone can actually hold, and therefore whether the shared deployment is a later config flip or a thing to do now. \"Probably tolerable\" is doing real work in that paragraph, and the failure mode is silent: nobody learns a link died except the person who stopped replying.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <legend>Item 2 — your position</legend>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"Per-dev is fine; host-independent identity is sufficient insurance\"><span><b>Leave it.</b> Per-dev clusters plus host-independent identity are enough. Revisit when someone actually needs an external link.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"Per-dev, but with an explicit internal-only rule written down\"><span><b>Leave it, but write the rule down.</b> Internal recipients only, stated in the docs, not just understood.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"Per-dev, with a technical guard against external links\"><span><b>Guard it technically.</b> Something in the product should make an external-stakeholder link hard or impossible, not just discouraged.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"Move to one shared deployment now\"><span><b>Move now.</b> Stand up the single shared deployment before anyone gets burned; the config flip is cheap, the incident isn't.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q2\" value=\"Other (see reasoning)\"><span><b>Other</b> — see my reasoning.</span></label>\n    <textarea name=\"q2why\" placeholder=\"Why. If you'd leave it, name the trigger that would force the move.\"></textarea>\n  </fieldset>\n</section>\n\n<!-- ITEM 3 -->\n<section class=\"item\">\n  <h2><span class=\"tag\">OPEN&nbsp;3</span>MCP server over the REST API</h2>\n\n  <h3>What exists</h3>\n  <div class=\"settled\">\n    <p>The REST API is built — routes in <code>README.md</code>. Bearer-authenticated, and it's what the participant-facing app uses too.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <h3>The proposal</h3>\n  <div class=\"contested\">\n    <p>An MCP server layered on top, exposing <code>list_widgets</code>, <code>create_brief</code>, <code>await_responses</code> as tools — the idiomatic agent-facing surface, removing the need for an agent to remember curl invocations.</p>\n    <p>One thing is already decided: <b>REST stays underneath either way</b>, because an orchestrator resuming a session is not necessarily an agent. So the question is purely timing and priority, not whether MCP replaces anything. Note that <code>await_responses</code> implies long polls, which is where an MCP surface and the edge path have to agree about timeouts.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <legend>Item 3 — your position</legend>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Build the MCP server now\"><span><b>Build it now.</b> The curl-invocation friction is the thing agents actually trip on.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Build it after items 1 and 2 resolve\"><span><b>Queue it.</b> Worth building, but after items 1 and 2 resolve.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Defer indefinitely — REST is sufficient for now\"><span><b>Defer.</b> REST is sufficient; revisit only if agents demonstrably struggle with it.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Build a reduced MCP surface first\"><span><b>Reduced surface first.</b> Ship a subset of the three tools; the rest can wait.</span></label>\n    <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"q3\" value=\"Other (see reasoning)\"><span><b>Other</b> — see my reasoning.</span></label>\n    <textarea name=\"q3why\" placeholder=\"Why. If you'd trim the surface, say which tools ship first and how await_responses handles long polls.\"></textarea>\n  </fieldset>\n</section>\n\n<!-- FORM META -->\n<section class=\"item\">\n  <h2>Your submission</h2>\n  <form id=\"f\">\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>Who is answering</legend>\n      <div class=\"who\">\n        <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"who\" value=\"Priya\"><span>Priya</span></label>\n        <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"who\" value=\"Sam\"><span>Sam</span></label>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"hint\">Both maintainers must submit separately. Fill this in, generate your summary, and paste it into the thread.</p>\n    </fieldset>\n\n    <fieldset>\n      <legend>Anything else</legend>\n      <div class=\"row\">\n        <div>\n          <label class=\"hint\" for=\"dep\">Item you'd want settled first</label>\n          <input type=\"text\" id=\"dep\" name=\"dep\" placeholder=\"e.g. Item 1, before anything else\">\n        </div>\n        <div>\n          <label class=\"hint\" for=\"date\">Date</label>\n          <input type=\"text\" id=\"date\" name=\"date\" placeholder=\"YYYY-MM-DD\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <textarea name=\"general\" placeholder=\"Objections to how the argument has been framed above, missing options, or anything the doc got wrong.\"></textarea>\n    </fieldset>\n\n    <div class=\"actions\">\n      <button type=\"button\" id=\"gen\">Generate summary</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost\" id=\"dl\">Download as .md</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost\" id=\"clear\">Clear form</button>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"out\">\n      <h3>Copy this into the thread</h3>\n      <textarea id=\"outText\" readonly></textarea>\n      <div class=\"actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost\" id=\"copy\">Copy to clipboard</button></div>\n    </div>\n  </form>\n</section>\n\n<footer>Source: <code>docs/DESIGN.md</code>, quoted verbatim in the boxed passages. Positions collected here are advisory until both maintainers have answered every item.</footer>\n\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var items = [\n    { key: \"q1\", title: \"Item 1 — The core bet: a schema, not a framework\" },\n    { key: \"q2\", title: \"Item 2 — The per-dev cluster problem\" },\n    { key: \"q3\", title: \"Item 3 — MCP server over the REST API\" }\n  ];\n\n  function pick(name) {\n    var el = document.querySelector('input[name=\"' + name + '\"]:checked');\n    return el ? el.value : \"(no position given)\";\n  }\n  function val(name) {\n    var el = document.querySelector('[name=\"' + name + '\"]');\n    return el && el.value.trim() ? el.value.trim() : \"\";\n  }\n\n  function build() {\n    var who = pick(\"who\");\n    var lines = [];\n    lines.push(\"# Positions on docs/DESIGN.md open items\");\n    lines.push(\"\");\n    lines.push(\"**Maintainer:** \" + who);\n    if (val(\"date\")) lines.push(\"**Date:** \" + val(\"date\"));\n    lines.push(\"\");\n    items.forEach(function (it) {\n      lines.push(\"## \" + it.title);\n      lines.push(\"\");\n      lines.push(\"**Position:** \" + pick(it.key));\n      lines.push(\"\");\n      lines.push(\"**Reasoning:** \" + (val(it.key + \"why\") || \"(none given)\"));\n      lines.push(\"\");\n    });\n    if (val(\"dep\")) {\n      lines.push(\"## Sequencing\");\n      lines.push(\"\");\n      lines.push(\"Settle first: \" + val(\"dep\"));\n      lines.push(\"\");\n    }\n    if (val(\"general\")) {\n      lines.push(\"## Other comments\");\n      lines.push(\"\");\n      lines.push(val(\"general\"));\n      lines.push(\"\");\n    }\n    var missing = items.filter(function (it) {\n      return !document.querySelector('input[name=\"' + it.key + '\"]:checked');\n    }).map(function (it) { return it.title.split(\" — \")[0]; });\n    if (missing.length || who === \"(no position given)\") {\n      lines.push(\"---\");\n      lines.push(\"\");\n      lines.push(\"_Incomplete: \" +\n        (who === \"(no position given)\" ? \"no maintainer selected. \" : \"\") +\n        (missing.length ? \"no position on \" + missing.join(\", \") + \".\" : \"\") + \"_\");\n    }\n    return lines.join(\"\\n\");\n  }\n\n  document.getElementById(\"gen\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    document.getElementById(\"outText\").value = build();\n    document.getElementById(\"out\").style.display = \"block\";\n    document.getElementById(\"out\").scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\", block: \"start\" });\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById(\"copy\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    var t = document.getElementById(\"outText\");\n    t.select();\n    try { document.execCommand(\"copy\"); this.textContent = \"Copied\"; } catch (e) { this.textContent = \"Select and copy manually\"; }\n    var b = this;\n    setTimeout(function () { b.textContent = \"Copy to clipboard\"; }, 1800);\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById(\"dl\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    var who = pick(\"who\").toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]/g, \"\") || \"unsigned\";\n    var blob = new Blob([build()], { type: \"text/markdown\" });\n    var a = document.createElement(\"a\");\n    a.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob);\n    a.download = \"design-positions-\" + who + \".md\";\n    document.body.appendChild(a);\n    a.click();\n    document.body.removeChild(a);\n    setTimeout(function(){ URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href); }, 1000);\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById(\"clear\").addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    document.getElementById(\"f\").reset();\n    document.querySelectorAll('input[type=radio]').forEach(function (r) { r.checked = false; });\n    document.querySelectorAll('textarea').forEach(function (t) { if (t.id !== \"outText\") t.value = \"\"; });\n    document.getElementById(\"out\").style.display = \"none\";\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>"
}
